  "notes": "The final contract is 5♥. West's lead of the ♠K, attacking dummy's entries, looks like a good start for the defense. West is marked with the ♣A for his takeout double making prospects of playing on that suit dubious. Trumps will have to be 3-2 for the contract to have a chance. South's basic plan should be to use dummy's diamonds for club discards. If diamonds are 4-1, South must be careful.\n\nIf South wins the ♠A and cashes the ♥A and ♥Q before unblocking in diamonds, East might be able to ruff and the defense will quickly take 2 club tricks.\n\nSouth can guard against the above distribution by allowing West to win at trick 1. West can do no better than continue spades on which South can discard 1 of the blocking diamonds.\n\nThe ♥A and ♥Q are cashed. South unblocks his remaining diamond and draws the last trump with the ♥K. Dummy's diamonds will provide discards for all of South's clubs and the contract will make with an overtrick (West could have cashed the ♣A to hold the overtrick).",
